{"id": "EUVD-2026-82051", "enisaUuid": "57df56f4-55a1-3bde-93b1-2922c97ba8dc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/bitmap: resume array on backlog_store() error path\n\nbacklog_store() suspends the array before checking whether a write-mostly\ndevice exists. If no such device exists, the error path only unlocks\nreconfig_mutex and leaves the array suspended, blocking subsequent I/O.\n\nUse mddev_unlock_and_resume() to release both states.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03aad318f0a1f039dddf98739e705fdca3bf0d86", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6763fb409a0b4106676a52cf934440d9484b32c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc543e769b97d563b089b9e0ebf8ad361d15076f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2911cd0a0f4366a7e06832bc5f0a7fdcc138e4dc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90390", "GHSA-xj4x-xc4w-3c2g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0db5e8e7-568f-328f-ba81-bc78c2456136", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "58226942ad3d1423785f815ede5bcc832574f2ea <2911cd0a0f4366a7e06832bc5f0a7fdcc138e4dc"}, {"id": "1262b9c4-2041-3140-9efc-f29213b69574", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "3e70a9cf-e0fd-3a2d-bc3b-6398970f4ca2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "58226942ad3d1423785f815ede5bcc832574f2ea <cc543e769b97d563b089b9e0ebf8ad361d15076f"}, {"id": "50c86229-97d7-3d30-9424-d8be7b969980", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "6b6d017c-cb25-3a67-9aa0-45691540e36e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "aa1df347-033d-3864-86b3-a5e464354262", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.